st Democrat Annie Andrews. The state's Republican lean and the absence of any Democratic Senate win since 1998 frame the contest, but the race has drawn unexpected attention as polls show a closer contest than the partisan baseline would suggest.\n\nAndrews has raised over $10 million to Graham's modest total, though outside groups have spent heavily to back Graham. Recent surveys show margins ranging from even to Graham +13, with most recent polls in the low single digits. Expert raters mostly call the race Likely Republican, though several shifted toward Lean Republican in late September. Prediction markets still give Andrews only about a one-in-seven chance, suggesting the race remains Graham's to lose.", "history": [{"date": "2026-09-22", "p_dem": 0.1565, "margin": -5.15}, {"date": "2026-09-23", "p_dem": 0.2122, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-24", "p_dem": 0.2115, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-25", "p_dem": 0.2143, "margin": -5.0}, {"date": "2026-09-26", "p_dem": 0.1474, "margin": -5.5}]}